  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In Shang clan city, Old Zhang reports that San Cha mountain has found how to enter the three kings inheritance ground.",
      "chapters": [
        324
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_shang_clan_city",
        "loc_san_cha_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan first steps through, he stands alone in a wilderness under a greyish white sky, on hard grey ground with yellow grass in the cracks, in dead silence with no wind or animal sound. The three kings inheritance sits inside a Gu Immortal blessed land rather than in the main world, and time there flows three times faster than outside. Other Gu besides Spring Autumn Cicada are suppressed by the small world’s laws, leaving only the rank one dog enslavement Gu usable at the start, and the same key-Gu rule applies to King Xin Inheritance and King Bao Inheritance with their own entry Gu. Early rounds open on ordinary wild dogs that are common in outside forests, and the first stage can hand a thin, knee-high wild dog with little battle strength.",
      "chapters": [
        346
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "path-rules-and-early-rounds",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "gu_spring_autumn_cicada",
        "gu_dog_enslavement_gu",
        "inh_king_xin_inheritance",
        "inh_king_bao_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Among the three kings, King Quan is an enslavement path Gu Master, and the inheritance is built to choose inheritors of that path. Difficulty rises sharply every ten rounds of battles. From the tenth round onward, dense grey fog offers choices such as chrysanthemum akita dog, lightning symbol dog, hedgedog, or another Gu Master as opponent.",
      "chapters": [
        347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "path-rules-and-early-rounds",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_king_quan",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The hedgedog’s body is full of spikes and its attack power is twice that of an ordinary dog, and without steel armor dogs or Yin dogs a challenger with few injured wild dogs is wise to avoid that path.",
      "chapters": [
        348
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "path-rules-and-early-rounds",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is a demonic path inheritance: Gu Masters may kill each other, and dead Gu Masters leave their Gu behind because blessed land law keeps those Gu from self-destructing.",
      "chapters": [
        347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "path-rules-and-early-rounds",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On the peaks of San Cha mountain, as more Gu Masters enter, the yellow light pillar shrinks until the doors close for that opening.",
      "chapters": [
        352
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "peak-pillars",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Among the three inheritances it is the one that depends most on luck, because a strong early dog group can snowball through later rounds. In one eighteenth-round run, Ku Mo already holds a jade eye dog king and a large steel armor dog group. Steel armor dogs have thick black leather armor and the greatest defense among dogs for the first fifty rounds. The jade eye dog king is a hundred beast king with a wild Gu effective against Yin dogs, whose formless bodies ordinary dogs cannot hit.",
      "chapters": [
        380
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "luck-and-snowball",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ku_mo",
        "sys_wild_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Under the land spirit’s guidance, Bai Ning Bing moves through King Quan Inheritance far more easily than when she explored alone.",
      "chapters": [
        382
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "late-dog-forces",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bai_ning_bing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan tells her that the last few rounds hold many lion mastiffs, mutated beasts stronger than the five great mountain dogs and once King Quan’s trump cards, plus two dog emperors that were his left and right arms, each able to match a rank five Gu Master.",
      "chapters": [
        387
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "late-dog-forces",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After Bai Ning Bing’s King Quan run she stands outside the blessed land’s central hall with nearly a hundred thousand dog beasts, while Feng Tian Yu reports receiving King Xin Inheritance; on San Cha mountain’s peak the yellow and blue pillars are gone, and talk says King Quan and King Xin Inheritance have been taken. Some name Wu Gui as the likely taker of King Quan Inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        389
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritances-taken",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_feng_tian_yu",
        "char_wu_gui"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo Wu Tian later names King Quan’s dog emperors as Ying Ming and Ba Huang.",
      "chapters": [
        391
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dog-emperors",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_mo_wu_tian",
        "char_ying_ming",
        "char_ba_huang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Bai Ning Bing commands both dog emperors when Mo Wu Tian and Xiao Mang press the dog line.",
      "chapters": [
        394
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dog-emperors",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_xiao_mang"
      ]
    }
  ],
